# .cursorrules

## Project
Multi-step-function migration workspace. Converting AWS Step Functions 
into synchronous TypeScript workflows in pharmacy-api-order-schedule.

## Skills (read before any migration task)
- .cursor/skills/sfn-analysis.md
- .cursor/skills/workflow-conventions.md
- .cursor/skills/migration-playbook.md

## Workspace Layout
- step_functions/ — ASL JSON files for all step functions being migrated
- dynamodb-config-test.csv — maps apiParamName constants to actual API URLs
- crm-common-api-handler/ — shared Lambda that proxies all HTTP calls 
  (DUMB PROXY — zero business logic, just resolves apiParamName via 
  DynamoDB and makes the HTTP call)
- pharmacy-api-order-schedule/ — TARGET repo where workflows land. 
  Uses a common-adapter dependency internally for making external HTTP calls.
- migration-analysis/ — per-step-function analysis artifacts

## Architecture
- Every step function calls crm-common-api-handler with:
  - apiParamName (constant like "get-memberships-benefits")
  - method (GET/POST)
  - queryParams or body
  - headers (passed through)
- crm-common-api-handler looks up apiParamName in DynamoDB → gets domain + path
- dynamodb-config-test.csv has this mapping — use it to resolve final URLs
- ALL business logic lives in the Step Function ASL:
  - Choice states = business rules / routing
  - Output/Parameters blocks with {% %} = data transforms
    (filtering, date comparisons, $uppercase, $filter, null coalescing)
  - Intrinsics wrap response data from deeply nested envelope:
    states.result.Payload.body.apiResponse.responseBody.{actual data}
- The target repo (pharmacy-api-order-schedule) uses common-adapter 
  for external calls — map API_CALL steps to the appropriate adapter

## Workflow Engine Step Types
- API_CALL — direct HTTP call via common-adapter (replaces Lambda proxy)
- RULE_CHECK — json-rules-engine rule (replaces Choice states)
- DATA_EXTRACTION — field extraction and transforms (replaces Output blocks)
- DATA_LOOKUP — reference data / config lookups
- DB_OPERATION — database reads/writes
- RUN_WORKFLOW — sub-workflow invocation

## Context Flow
- storeAs — saves step output to context
- $.references — reads from context
- RuleOutcome: CONTINUE, STOP_EXIT, FAIL_JOB, RUN_WORKFLOW

## Rules
- Every migration follows the 6-phase playbook
- API_CALL steps use common-adapter — no Lambda proxy, no DynamoDB lookup
- Inline ASL transforms (Output blocks) become separate DATA_EXTRACTION steps
- Choice states become RULE_CHECK with json-rules-engine
- Parallel states → flag (not yet supported)
- Data contract parity must be verified per element